{"duration_api_ms":170256,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"01850d5e-e07f-46fc-aa81-1f94d54f8f01","total_cost_usd":1.9266249999999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":62,"cache_creation_input_tokens":117484,"cache_read_input_tokens":3115925,"output_tokens":18166,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3855},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":117484,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1138,"cache_read_input_tokens":126674,"cache_creation_input_tokens":928,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":928},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":62,"outputTokens":18166,"cacheReadInputTokens":3115925,"cacheCreationInputTokens":117484,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.9266249999999998,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":3855,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":31,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Revision 2 of TASK-260830-nxqqaw goes back to the developer (`to-dev`): changes requested, one blocking finding. The finding repeats the rev1 problem at a new spot.\n\n**Blocking finding: `wireobject-response-member-names-case-folded` (bypass).** In `internal/merkleinventory/serve.go`, `decodeOneWireObject` only checks that a returned object has 4 members, then decodes it with Go's standard JSON decoder. That decoder matches member names regardless of case. So a hostile peer can answer `objects.get` with `{\"DATA\",\"Encoding\",\"Media_Type\",\"OBJECT_ID\"}` and `FetchObjects` accepts it. The spec's object shape has exactly `object_id`, `media_type`, `encoding`, `data`. A probe test I wrote reproduces it on the exact tree. Rev1's finding was the same kind of loose JSON decoding, on the request side, so this carries `repeat-of` rev1.\n\n**What I reran myself:**\n- **Full `go test ./...`:** green. `internal/specpin` fails in my archive copy only because the copy has no `.task-board`; it passes in the live worktree.\n- **Windows `go vet`, gofmt, `-count=3`:** vet exits 0, gofmt reports nothing, and the three touched packages pass three times.\n- **Registry and config:** `task-board.config.json` and the traceability registry are unchanged from base.\n- **Fixtures:** my own Python JCS + SHA-256 script gives the empty, singleton and branch roots, both branch child hashes, and all six MIXED-NS-1 roots exactly as the spec lists them.\n- **Importer outcome grid:** I compared every test across the 14 packages that import `canonicaljson`, base against candidate: 17,633 against 18,000 results, no failures on either side, nothing went from pass to fail. Only two old tests disappeared: the ones pinning that tombstone and tombstone-ack were refused. That matches the change the producer named: those two schemas are now accepted under §10.7.\n- **Shipped mutation harness:** run twice. Every mutant was caught both times, the harmless control survived, and the tree was restored.\n- **Rev1 issues:** all fixed. The request-type finding is closed, and the three uncaught mutants rev1 noted are now caught.\n\n**My own mutations:** 5 of 8 caught. Each of the 5 was also caught by its named test run alone, twice. The harmless control survived as it should. The 3 survivors are test gaps, not wrong behaviour, and are recorded as notes:\n- `fetchcbor`: nothing tests that the client refuses an object labelled `cbor` when it asked only for JSON.\n- `quarevent` and `quarall`: the quarantine check inside `ObjectsGet` can never fire, because quarantining already deletes the stored object. It should be removed or given a test.\n\nNot attacked: I did not add my own timestamp tie-break mutant; I relied on the shipped harness mutants, which were caught in both runs.\n\nThe verdict (`TASK-260830-nxqqaw_review-verdict-rev2.md`) and the evidence archive (`TASK-260830-nxqqaw_review-evidence-rev2.tar.gz`, 412 KB) are attached. I checked both against my local copies after upload. The review checklist items are ticked, and the scratch directory is deleted.","ttft_ms":1795,"type":"result","duration_ms":944295,"uuid":"dc518e69-4a78-45bb-8fd3-57c810b27a5c","ttft_stream_ms":1328,"time_to_request_ms":32,"first_content_frame_ms":1329,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
